{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the descendants of Reuben, firstborn of Israel.</b> Since at the journeying Judah was first, it gives here the reason why Reuben was counted first: because he was the firstborn of Israel." "<b>By the number of names, by their polls.</b> Why is 'by their polls' said regarding Reuben and Simon more than all the other tribes? Because Jacob rebuked them when he blessed his sons, and they required atonement. And regarding shekels that come for atonement it is written בקע לגלגלת."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:55.154343667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}